    "abstract": "<jats:p>In the title molecule, C<jats:sub>17</jats:sub>H<jats:sub>16</jats:sub>N<jats:sub>2</jats:sub>O<jats:sub>2</jats:sub>, the quinoxaline portion is slightly folded about the N...N axis with an angle of 4.27 (4)°. In the crystal, O—H...O and weak C—H...O hydrogen bonds link molecules along the <jats:italic>b-</jats:italic>axis direction. In addition, two sets of weak C—H...π(ring) interactions form a two-dimensional `step' motif parallel to the <jats:italic>bc</jats:italic> plane.</jats:p>",
